# Cloud Run / Docker build context exclusions for google-ai-studio/Dockerfile.
# Build context is repo root ("/") per GOOGLE_CLOUD_RUN_DEPLOYMENT.md, and the
# Dockerfile does `COPY . .` — without this file EVERYTHING on disk in this
# directory (or in whatever Cloud Build clones) is sent to the builder and
# baked into the image, including secrets that happen to sit on disk (.env),
# full git history, and ~1500 files this app never reads at runtime.
#
# Verified before adding each entry below: no runtime require()/readFile
# reference from server.js, api/, lib/, shared/, apps/dark-void-scene/, or
# google-ai-studio/cloudrun-entry.cjs into any of these paths (grepped the
# actual request-serving code paths, not just "looks unused").
#
# Kept in the image (do not add these without re-verifying runtime use):
#   data/, shared/, apps/, lib/, api/, google-ai-studio/, state/,
#   package.json, package-lock.json, server.js

# Version control / secrets — never let local disk state leak into an image layer.
.git/
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies — installed fresh by `RUN npm ci` in the Dockerfile; copying a
# host node_modules (e.g. from a local `docker build .`) would ship
# host-platform native binaries (sharp) into a Linux container.
node_modules/

# Dev/CI-only tooling and content — not on any request path the deployed
# container serves.
scripts/
supabase/
services/
systems/
tools/
test/
e2e/
docs/
.github/

# Large "not yet integrated" holding areas — self-contained patch bundles
# with their own manual INSTALL_TO_WORLD_SERVER.bat, not wired into
# server.js/apps/dark-void-scene. ~1500 files combined; biggest single
# contributor to build-context size.
.iw-graphics-staging/
WORLD_QUALITY_AUTOPILOT_V4_1_HOTFIX/
_IMPROVE_V1_TMP/
.texture-pipeline-backup/

# Build/test artifacts, caches, logs, archives.
node_modules/.cache/
.cache/
coverage/
test-results/
.pytest_cache/
*.log
*.zip
*.tmp-*

# Editor/OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
